{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal","id":1531275,"title":"The advantage of being Mortal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-22T01:09:49-08:00","id":1531275,"title":"The advantage of being Mortal","content":"I feel like being Mortal is actually pretty strong in CofD, you might not be as powerful as the Major Template Supernatural, but you don't have the baggae that come with being a Major Template, and having access to Supernatural Merit is nice, because some of the Supernatural Merit can't realI feel like being Mortal is actually pretty strong in CofD, you might not be as powerful as the Major Template Supernatural, but you don't have the baggage that come with being a Major Template, and having access to Supernatural Merit is nice, because some of the Supernatural Merit can't real be replicate as easily by the Major Template Power and even if the Major Template can replicate the power, Supernatural Merit cost less than the Major Template Power and have less drawback on their power, sure they can't go one to one with any of the Major Template, not even Hunter since those would have better gear than the average Mortal, but they have strength in being one of the Mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T01:48:21-08:00","id":1531276,"title":"","content":"&quot;This Guy spittin facts&quot;<br /> Promethean Rapper<br /> no but seriously i agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T02:28:48-08:00","id":1531280,"title":"","content":"Did they add new emoji to the forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T04:29:19-08:00","id":1531287,"title":"","content":"Mortals do posses a few advantages, but their primary advantages are two things. First, on a big scale, numbers. They outnumber the other splats probably tens of thousands to 1. That doesn't help on a personal scale but it is a huge advantage. <br /> <br /> On a personal scale their biggest advantage is being underestimated. Supernatural merits don't typically rise to the power level of supernatural powers, but then monsters likely aren't expecting any supernatural ability at all from a human. <br /> <br /> Does that make them individually strong? Not really. They're probably the weakest thing in CofD on a personal level. But it does mean that a clever mortal, or even a not clever one with the right trick or two, can turn the tables on a supernatural foe. <br /> <br /> Of course there's also a level that's neither personal nor relying on strength of numbers and that's a more background type level where people are using things like resources, allies, contacts, and status to oppose one another and at that level mortals can do very well indeed. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T06:24:15-08:00","id":1531289,"title":"","content":"I want to see more organization that is similiar to Hunter without being Hunter, that show Mortal not being innocent victim of the supernatural, but a part of the darkness that people often don't see or focus on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T07:05:04-08:00","id":1531290,"title":"","content":"&quot;A seasoned occultist should not be underestimated. The very best take the time to build esoteric armories, carefully curate their personal occult libraries, build their workshops, hire the very best Retainers to engineer gear that would impress Lucius Fox himself. Those are the hallowed heights that await you.<br /> <br /> Sure, its a lot more work to learn some Ceremonies or bind Familiars than it is to become a leading expert in a profession and live comfortably. But a world beyond the world is now open to you, with challenges and treasures awaiting someone with the focus, preparation and indomitable will to seize them.<br /> <br /> Remember, all the greats started where you are now and it was sharp wits that saw them through. A bunch of vampires might strut like they own the place, but hit them with a balloons filled with gasoline, light em' up with a flare gun and their confidence dissolves into panic. In time we will teach you many more methods, but for now, we welcome you to our occult security corporation. Your time with us will be many things, but never boring.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-22-2024, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T09:14:17-08:00","id":1531293,"title":"","content":"Supernatural merits absolutely come with baggage. They're generic mechanics that you can reskin, so how they function and what limitations they have as a result are for that reason not generally described mechanically.<br /> <br /> To give an example: <i>Laying on Hands</i>. The merit itself says that it's somehow related to the character's faith or devotion. Logically that suggests that the character has to maintain that faith/devotion or the power goes away. It's not mentioned in the merit, it's a feature of the narrative.<br /> <br /> The big part of being a template is that narratively you have an easy justification for buying more powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T09:38:41-08:00","id":1531295,"title":"","content":"That felt more like a Hunter Organization than a Mortal one, I feel a Mortal Organization are one that instead of fighting the Darkness to protect humanity, they can go either way, but they're mostly interested in their own cause, they aren't hunter because they don't battle the Darkness, they live with the Darkness, I can think of 5 Mortal Organization philososhy.<br /> 1. Embrace the Darkness: The Darkness is a part of the World, which mean it's a part of you as well, why try to deny it, when you can become a part of it? <br /> Example: A group of Occultist wanting to be possessd.<br /> 2. Live with the Darkness: The Darkness is everywhere, you can't really ignore it, so, the best you can do is try to live with the Darkness.<br /> Example: A Family greet a new Vampire neighbor, directing him to a souce of blood that isn't their own.<br /> 3. Ignore the Darkness: The Darkness is wide spread, but it isn't everywhere, you can always find a place without the taint of the Darkness, a place you can call home.<br /> Example: A Online Forum reviewing what is the least haunted street in London.<br /> 4. Worship the Darkness: The Darkness is strong, it's potent, with raw energy, it's the form of true divinity, human should fear, respect, and desire it, for it is Divine.<br /> Example: A Cult of whoese pantheon are made of 3 Vampire, 2 Werewolves, and 1 Sin-Eater.<br /> 5. Exploit the Darkness: The Darkness is rich, with untap potential, that no one have Monopoly in, and the Market demand what can't be obtain.<br /> Example: A Company dedicating to collect Ghost Essence for spiritual healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T16:25:58-08:00","id":1531318,"title":"","content":"It's true that as a human you have the advantages of not having obvious weaknesses like sunlight or needing to hunt to survive. But considering that you know that this exists, I believe you would feel insecure at the very least, after all the supernaturals are much stronger and it wouldn't be strange for one of them to have an inflated ego and kill you on a whim, hunger, or just because he had a On a bad day, there are those who would say that it is similar to facing an armed person, but an armed person can still be held responsible and arrested if they kill you, besides, you can also arm yourself and leave the fight &quot;even&quot;, but a supernatural person would not be caught so easy and even if it were it's likely he could beat them easily. So yeah, being a human being is complicated in this case, you can argue that supernaturals would die if they just unlived people left and right and made their existence obvious, but every now and then it's still viable, you can live happily if you're oblivious to these events, but being at the base of the pyramid means that you are the weakest and will be treated as the weakest.<br /> <br /> Now going through this issue of powers, not much to complement, you have the advantage of not being so inconvenient, but you will still be weaker most of the time, so if you happen to attract the attention of someone you shouldn't, you would still be defeated or used, so good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T17:15:33-08:00","id":1531323,"title":"","content":"Mortal with Supernatural Merit aren't common, but I belive that every Mortal have the potential to have at least 1 Supernatural Merit. Supernatural Merit have 3 origin, Come from the Inner self, Come from the Outer influence, Come from both the Inner and Outer, Human Soul are magical so the Inner self part is easy, the World is magical so the Outer Influencd part is also easy, the Human Soul regulary interact with the World magical energy so that is also easy, it's just that Mortal tend to not stay alive to have enough power or too afraid to embrace that Supernatural power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T17:29:56-08:00","id":1531325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531295#post1531295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That felt more like a Hunter Organization than a Mortal one, I feel a Mortal Organization are one that instead of fighting the Darkness to protect humanity, they can go either way, but they're mostly interested in their own cause, they aren't hunter because they don't battle the Darkness, they live with the Darkness, I can think of 5 Mortal Organization philososhy.<br /> <br /> 1. Embrace the Darkness: The Darkness is a part of the World, which mean it's a part of you as well, why try to deny it, when you can become a part of it?<br /> Example: A group of Occultist wanting to be possessd.<br /> 2. Live with the Darkness: The Darkness is everywhere, you can't really ignore it, so, the best you can do is try to live with the Darkness.<br /> Example: A Family greet a new Vampire neighbor, directing him to a souce of blood that isn't their own.<br /> 3. Ignore the Darkness: The Darkness is wide spread, but it isn't everywhere, you can always find a place without the taint of the Darkness, a place you can call home.<br /> Example: A Online Forum reviewing what is the least haunted street in London.<br /> 4. Worship the Darkness: The Darkness is strong, it's potent, with raw energy, it's the form of true divinity, human should fear, respect, and desire it, for it is Divine.<br /> Example: A Cult of whoese pantheon are made of 3 Vampire, 2 Werewolves, and 1 Sin-Eater.<br /> 5. Exploit the Darkness: The Darkness is rich, with untap potential, that no one have Monopoly in, and the Market demand what can't be obtain.<br /> Example: A Company dedicating to collect Ghost Essence for spiritual healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.You described some ghouls wanting to be promoted, deviant autourgics, conspiracies, and there may be more, but I don't remember at the moment.<br /> <br /> 2.This is actually interesting, it would be a good topic for discussion on what it would be like to try to live with supernaturals and the situations that would unfold from that. I'll elaborate later.<br /> <br /> 3.It's funny... you writing like this I think of a series in which there is that classic American family from the 50s of a husband and wife with two children, living in a trailer looking for a normal city where they can simply have a peaceful life, but they always run into in a supernatural problem that they have to deal just to leave the city later and look for another place. We would have a husband who just want to read a newspaper in the morning, have lunch with the family and end the day by watching TV and going to sleep, but he cannot end a day without having to kill a werewolf that appeared in the garden, kick out an intruder or some beggar changeling coming to fill his patience by asking for alms; The mother who just wants to have friends to talk to, but they just want to use her as a quick snack, camouflage or an etiquette lesson; the eldest daughter who from time to time is dating some supernatural who isn't worth the air he breathe (if he breath) and that's why the father has to intervene; and lastly the youngest son who barely speaks a sentence a day and is so intelligent and cold-blooded that while his classmate, who happened to be an unfleashed, was telling his moving story of creation, he turned it off halfway through and used the components to make a new antenna, a toaster and repair the dishwasher. Yes, that was specific and it certainly wouldn't be the way we would like CofD to be presented in a possible series, but it would be funny.<br /> <br /> 4.I like to know how this pantheon works. The three vampires are incarnations of three brothers who were gods and were cursed by their father who believes he was cheated by his wife and now cannot walk under the sun, the werewolves are guardians provided by their mother and the sin-eater is the descendant of a priest who did worshiped them? No, seriously, is something like that?<br /> <br /> 5.I thought of something similar, but more along the lines of since they're not human I don't need to treat them as such and more along the lines of an evil company, but this goes more towards Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T18:44:09-08:00","id":1531329,"title":"","content":"I wanted to touch on embrace and worship the darkness. A good example of that is Shadow Occultists, people who were possessed or claimed once upon a time and who, having had their eyes opened to that world choose to seek out spirits and serve them. In exchange they get a portion of the spirit's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T02:41:27-08:00","id":1531341,"title":"","content":"Shadow Occultists are a great example, but they do become something of a minor template, and arguable no longer mortals. I really like having mortals join a Pack, but with no werewolves in it...<br /> <br /> It would be similar with the Sons of Phobos or Purified, or Eaters of the Dead.<br /> <br /> I think a Necromancer's cult would still be wholely mortal, just with access to some mementos and ceremonies.<br /> <br /> Or a group of Shamans without debasing themselves, but with various spirit pacts/magical tools.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go with 6. It isn't darkness, it is good actually, and we shouldn't be afraid. Maybe catalogues the Darkness to help understand it, possibly joining the Mysterium as sleepwalkers and going on expeditions...<br /> <br /> Maybe a online group gathering various magical knowledge, looking for Shamans with spirit knowledge, cult/ex-cult members with Sorcerous rites, Necromancers with various ceremonies, some groups trying to explore the hedge and return safely with goblin fruit/Icons.<br /> <br /> These groups actually believe that it can't be that bad, and keep pushing despite the occasional dissapearance of one of their members.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T04:36:33-08:00","id":1531343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531341#post1531341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Occultists are a great example, but they do become something of a minor template, and arguable no longer mortals. I really like having mortals join a Pack, but with no werewolves in it...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Supernatural Merit Template exist and is still technically just a Mortal, so I think that 'Embrace the Darkness' Mortal Organization are people who want to become part of a Supernatural Merit Template of somekind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5.I thought of something similar, but more along the lines of since they're not human I don't need to treat them as such and more along the lines of an evil company, but this goes more towards Hunter. </div> </div> </div>That is definetly more of a hunter Organization, I was thinking more like they don't only use The Darkness as resource, they also deal with the Darkness.<br /> <br /> I think the Mortal Organization are much more blatanly morally grey, since instead of fighting against it, they have more selfish goal.<br /> <br /> Embrace the Darkness: They only embrace it, because they don't want to be the prey of it, being within it, give you some power you wouldn't have otherwise.<br /> <br /> Live with the Darkness: They use other Mortal as pawn to raise their reputation up in the Supernatural Society, making sure that nobody harm them, and for those that do, get what comming to them, they see the Darkness as equal, not something to be worship.<br /> <br /> Ignore the Darkness: They willfully ignore the Darkness, even as it's eating their neighbor, as long as people their care about and the organization they are in are safe, they don't need to make life more complicated than it already is.<br /> <br /> Worship the Darkness: While they're similiar to 'Embrace the Darkness' they view becoming one with The Darkness, as becoming one witht the Divine, dangerous and risky, it can make you mad, or lose anything that resemble your former self, instead they choose to appease the Darkness and gain the power that way.<br /> <br /> Exploit the Darkness: They only care about the profit, it's not only money, it's can be powerful artifact, contact, land, title, anything that have some sort of value, they view the Darkness as resouce to be harvest and use, but so are everything else that isn't them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531341#post1531341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go with 6. It isn't darkness, it is good actually, and we shouldn't be afraid. Maybe catalogues the Darkness to help understand it, possibly joining the Mysterium as sleepwalkers and going on expeditions...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How should this sixth type of Mortal Organization be called? Study the Darkness? And how are they morally grey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T04:48:01-08:00","id":1531345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531341#post1531341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Occultists are a great example, but they do become something of a minor template, and arguable no longer mortals. I really like having mortals join a Pack, but with no werewolves in it...<br /> <br /> It would be similar with the Sons of Phobos or Purified, or Eaters of the Dead.<br /> <br /> I think a Necromancer's cult would still be wholely mortal, just with access to some mementos and ceremonies.<br /> <br /> Or a group of Shamans without debasing themselves, but with various spirit pacts/magical tools.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go with 6. It isn't darkness, it is good actually, and we shouldn't be afraid. Maybe catalogues the Darkness to help understand it, possibly joining the Mysterium as sleepwalkers and going on expeditions...<br /> <br /> Maybe a online group gathering various magical knowledge, looking for Shamans with spirit knowledge, cult/ex-cult members with Sorcerous rites, Necromancers with various ceremonies, some groups trying to explore the hedge and return safely with goblin fruit/Icons.<br /> <br /> These groups actually believe that it can't be that bad, and keep pushing despite the occasional dissapearance of one of their members.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't &quot;become a template&quot; and given the requirements are &quot;human only&quot; and that you lose merits if you no longer meet the requirements I don't know how you would ever think they were anything but human. <br /> <br /> And no, it isn't &quot;like the Purified&quot; the Purified are immortals and involve you adding the Immortal template. Shadow Occultists are supernatural merits you purchase. They have a similar theme, but they are, mechanically, radically different. <br /> <br /> And comparing them to Eaters if the Dead is even more laughable. Eaters of the Dead are a Lodge, not a template, not a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T05:47:06-08:00","id":1531346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531345#post1531345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And comparing them to Eaters if the Dead is even more laughable. Eaters of the Dead are a Lodge, not a template, not a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orathaic is referring to the Eaters of the Dead from Geist, with their Cuisines and potential Abmortality. They're a template whose example Dread Powers include &quot;take Supernatural Merits appropriate to your ghost-eating idiom as Dread Powers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:04:27-08:00","id":1531348,"title":"","content":"I forget how often things share the exact same name sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T10:35:05-08:00","id":1531365,"title":"","content":"I feel like you're going overboard with categorization with mortals<br /> <br /> hunters ARE Mortals. The vigil involves, quite explicitly, anything from killing, exploitation, purification, rehabilitation, to even worship as Shulpae proves. A Hunter is simply a Mortal who's developed a Code to become more resilient to the supernatural horrors they intentionally go out to find","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T02:23:10-08:00","id":1531416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531275-the-advantage-of-being-mortal?p=1531343#post1531343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should this sixth type of Mortal Organization be called? Study the Darkness? And how are they morally grey?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, maybe they are just Embrace the darkness, but in denial/naive.<br /> <br /> Or &quot;What Darkness?&quot;<br /> <br /> They are not morally grey, they are dangerously blind to the risks. This can be incredibly dangerous, pushing people to explore stuff they barely have the capacity to handle, encouraging people online with the half-truths they have discovered and unearned confidence.<br /> <br /> They are risk blind.<br /> <br /> Could actually be a Hunter faction, given what was said about mortal organisations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T02:24:28-08:00","id":1531417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-ic